WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.139 --> 00:00:01.641
- Welcome to auction school!

00:00:01.641 --> 00:00:03.858
(upbeat banjo music)

00:00:03.858 --> 00:00:05.891
- 11 dollar bid and now 12,
now 12, who'll gimme 12?

00:00:05.891 --> 00:00:07.437
- [Group] Five, five,
five, five and a quarter,

00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:09.119
five and a quarter, five
and a half, five and a half,

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:10.585
- Will you give me 20,
will you give me 20?

00:00:10.585 --> 00:00:11.848
10, 10, 20, 20.

00:00:11.848 --> 00:00:13.354
- [Group] Eight and a
quarter, eight and a quarter,

00:00:13.354 --> 00:00:15.024
nine, nine, nine and a quarter.

00:00:15.024 --> 00:00:18.565
10 and a half, 10 and a
half, 75, 75, sold!

00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:21.615
- Give yourselves a hand, good job!

00:00:21.615 --> 00:00:24.261
- What 5,000, what five,
and I want one, five, two.

00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:25.647
- Here biddin' a two, here
biddin' a two and three

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:26.663
three and four, here biddin',

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:29.145
- Sold to buyer number 122,
here we go, rock and roll.

00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:30.368
- The Missouri Auction School was founded

00:00:30.368 --> 00:00:32.591
in 1905, it's the oldest and largest

00:00:32.591 --> 00:00:34.421
auction school in the world.

00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:36.739
It trains auctioneers in
every aspect of the auction

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:40.275
profession and is known as
the Harvard of auctioneering.

00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:42.638
- Introduce the item,
as for 10, drop to five,

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:45.201
I'll give you the five,
and then go to six.

00:00:45.201 --> 00:00:47.199
So we start every
morning at auction school

00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:49.230
with group drills.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.289
- [Group] Betty Botter bough some butter.

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:51.588
Buddy said his butter's bitter.

00:00:51.588 --> 00:00:53.176
Eight and a quarter, eight and a quarter,

00:00:53.176 --> 00:00:56.609
eight and half, eight and
half, 90, 90, 80, 80, 70, 70.

00:00:56.609 --> 00:00:59.539
- Just like an athlete would
warm up, we need to warm up.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:03.276
Very good, okay, give
yourselves a hand, good job!

00:01:03.276 --> 00:01:05.552
At auction school, the
most important aspect

00:01:05.552 --> 00:01:06.774
is that auction chant.

00:01:06.774 --> 00:01:08.239
- At a 100, now get a-two, three.

00:01:08.239 --> 00:01:09.421
- One dollar bid and now two, now two.

00:01:09.421 --> 00:01:10.563
- Two dollar bid and now three and three.

00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:13.772
- 20 dollar bid, now 25, 25 now, and sold.

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:16.253
- It's the very foundation
of the auction profession.

00:01:16.253 --> 00:01:18.047
I'm at 20 dollar bid and now 30, now 30,

00:01:18.047 --> 00:01:19.917
will you gimme 30, I'm at 20 dollar bid.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:20.849
Okay, let's try that.

00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:23.204
The auction chant is two
numbers, the money that you

00:01:23.204 --> 00:01:26.046
have bid and the money
that you're asking for.

00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:29.467
I have one dollar bid, now two,
now two, will you gimme two?

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.659
- I'm at two dollar bid and now three,

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:31.920
now three, will you gimme three?

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:32.817
I'm at two dollar bid.

00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:34.784
- Will you gimme 20,
will you you gimme 20?

00:01:34.784 --> 00:01:35.718
- Feel that?

00:01:35.718 --> 00:01:38.375
- Now 50, now 50 will you gimme 50?

00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:39.557
That's it, that's it!

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:40.390
Good job!

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.236
And as they sell more and
more, those filler words

00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:43.718
will slur so it'll move
a little bit faster.

00:01:43.718 --> 00:01:45.437
- A dollar 70, dollar 70,
dollar bid and now one,

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:46.500
now one dollar bid and now two.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.638
- 17, 17, will you gimme 17?

00:01:47.638 --> 00:01:49.629
Got a dollar 16, 17, 17 will you gimme 17?

00:01:49.629 --> 00:01:51.782
- Will you gimme 42, I'm
at 41, will you gimme 42,

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:53.126
I'm at 42, thank you sir.

00:01:53.126 --> 00:01:56.953
- I'm at 400, even 400
dollar, four, sold, 375!

00:01:56.953 --> 00:02:00.477
And that's what creates that
nice smooth rhythm chant.

00:02:00.477 --> 00:02:03.056
- Rubber baby buggy
bumper, basic rhythm, 'kay?

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.974
- Learning the auction
chant in a classroom setting

00:02:04.974 --> 00:02:07.332
is important, but you're
not really an auctioneer

00:02:07.332 --> 00:02:09.572
until you get to go to a real auction

00:02:09.572 --> 00:02:11.203
and sell real items to real people.

00:02:11.203 --> 00:02:12.383
- Dollar's five, somebody bid six dollars,

00:02:12.383 --> 00:02:13.216
who woulda bid six?

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.169
- [Baseball Cap] Dollar bid--
- [Striped Shirt] Yup!

00:02:14.169 --> 00:02:15.430
- She said three, she said three.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.018
- Five dollar, woulda bid six
dollars, who woulda bid six?

00:02:17.018 --> 00:02:17.914
Five, someone'd bid six?

00:02:17.914 --> 00:02:19.417
- Yup!

00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:20.881
- Sold, five dollars your way.

00:02:20.881 --> 00:02:23.113
- So at the student auction,
you never know what's gonna

00:02:23.113 --> 00:02:26.042
come up for sale and so you
gotta be ready for anything.

00:02:26.042 --> 00:02:29.459
- First item's lot 75, you
got a stack of three turtles.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:30.805
- We got an old tablecloth.

00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:32.554
- Jumper cables, very useful.

00:02:32.554 --> 00:02:33.735
- Ooh, a cuckoo clock!

00:02:33.735 --> 00:02:35.604
- It looks like another stack of turtles.

00:02:35.604 --> 00:02:39.310
- Lot number 663, it's a meat cleaver.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.143
- Yup!

00:02:41.837 --> 00:02:43.220
- So one of the most fascinating aspects

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.416
of the process is the transformation

00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:47.742
that the students make
throughout the program.

00:02:47.742 --> 00:02:49.938
So often when they first
come to the school,

00:02:49.938 --> 00:02:52.217
they're hesitant, they aren't
sure what they're doing.

00:02:52.217 --> 00:02:54.169
A lot of them are frightened, even.

00:02:54.169 --> 00:02:56.731
Once they get up and they
sell and they realize,

00:02:56.731 --> 00:02:59.864
"Yes, I can do this,
I can really do this!"

00:02:59.864 --> 00:03:02.422
You can hear it in their
voice, "I'm an auctioneer."

00:03:02.422 --> 00:03:03.750
- 15 dollar bid and now 20, now 20,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.294
would you gimme 20 bid, now 25.

00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:06.759
- Give yourselves a hand, great job.

00:03:06.759 --> 00:03:08.061
(clapping)

00:03:08.061 --> 00:03:09.850
That was really good.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.703
Good job.

00:03:10.703 --> 00:03:11.925
Okay, now let's do the chant.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:15.425
We'll go up to nine, we'll come back down.

